# Build-context filter for the Trade-Agent dev image.
#
# The image does NOT COPY the repository: the container gets its code from the
# `trade-workspace` named volume, populated by `scripts/dev-sync.sh` (one-way
# rsync from the read-only /src-ro bind). The Dockerfile is therefore the only
# file the build actually needs.
#
# This file only governs what the Docker *CLI* sends to the daemon as build
# context. Excluding everything keeps the context tiny and guarantees no host
# artifact (node_modules, .venv, backend/data, tool state, ...) can ever leak
# into an image layer. Order matters: the last matching pattern wins, so the
# `!` exceptions re-include the only files the build requires: the Dockerfile
# and the supervisor script it COPYs (docker/entrypoint.sh). The `docker`
# directory itself must be re-included before its file (a file cannot be
# re-included while its parent stays excluded).
**
!Dockerfile
!docker
!docker/entrypoint.sh
